title: FlexRender (Vanilla) Guide
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Vanilla adapter does not own a rendering engine. Its rendering helpers resolve plain column-definition values and functions, while your application decides how to turn the returned value into DOM nodes or HTML."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Import the helpers from the dedicated core entry point:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { FlexRender, flexRender } from '@tanstack/table-core/flex-render'","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"flexrender-vs-flexrender","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FlexRender"},{"type":"text","value":" vs "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"flexRender"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FlexRender"},{"type":"text","value":" is the table-aware wrapper. Pass exactly one "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cell"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"header"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"footer"},{"type":"text","value":" object:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const headerContent = header.isPlaceholder ? null : FlexRender({ header })\nconst cellContent = FlexRender({ cell })\nconst footerContent = FlexRender({ footer: header })","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For cells, it selects "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"aggregatedCell"},{"type":"text","value":" for aggregated rows, falls back to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cell"},{"type":"text","value":", and returns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"},{"type":"text","value":" for grouping placeholders."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"flexRender"},{"type":"text","value":" is the lower-level function for a renderable definition and its context:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const content = flexRender(cell.column.columnDef.cell, cell.getContext())","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"It invokes a function definition with the supplied props and passes any other value through unchanged. It does not select grouped-cell definitions or suppress placeholders."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Neither helper inserts content into the document. Handle the returned value according to your rendering system. For example, assign trusted text to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"textContent"},{"type":"text","value":", append a returned node, or pass a framework-specific value to another renderer. Do not assign untrusted strings to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"innerHTML"},{"type":"text","value":" without sanitizing them."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Placeholder headers and footers remain the caller's layout decision. Skip "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"header.isPlaceholder"},{"type":"text","value":" in ordinary layouts unless a spanning-header layout intentionally needs that content."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"flexrender-vs-flexrender","text":"FlexRender vs flexRender","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThe Vanilla adapter does not own a rendering engine. Its rendering helpers resolve plain column-definition values and functions, while your application decides how to turn the returned value into DOM nodes or HTML.\n\nImport the helpers from the dedicated core entry point:\n\n```ts\nimport { FlexRender, flexRender } from '@tanstack/table-core/flex-render'\n```\n\n## `FlexRender` vs `flexRender`\n\n`FlexRender` is the table-aware wrapper. Pass exactly one `cell`, `header`, or `footer` object:\n\n```ts\nconst headerContent = header.isPlaceholder ? null : FlexRender({ header })\nconst cellContent = FlexRender({ cell })\nconst footerContent = FlexRender({ footer: header })\n```\n\nFor cells, it selects `aggregatedCell` for aggregated rows, falls back to `cell`, and returns `null` for grouping placeholders.\n\n`flexRender` is the lower-level function for a renderable definition and its context:\n\n```ts\nconst content = flexRender(cell.column.columnDef.cell, cell.getContext())\n```\n\nIt invokes a function definition with the supplied props and passes any other value through unchanged. It does not select grouped-cell definitions or suppress placeholders.\n\nNeither helper inserts content into the document. Handle the returned value according to your rendering system. For example, assign trusted text to `textContent`, append a returned node, or pass a framework-specific value to another renderer. Do not assign untrusted strings to `innerHTML` without sanitizing them.\n\nPlaceholder headers and footers remain the caller's layout decision. Skip `header.isPlaceholder` in ordinary layouts unless a spanning-header layout intentionally needs that content.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: FlexRender (Vanilla) Guide\n---\n\nThe Vanilla adapter does not own a rendering engine. Its rendering helpers resolve plain column-definition values and functions, while your application decides how to turn the returned value into DOM nodes or HTML.\n\nImport the helpers from the dedicated core entry point:\n\n```ts\nimport { FlexRender, flexRender } from '@tanstack/table-core/flex-render'\n```\n\n## `FlexRender` vs `flexRender`\n\n`FlexRender` is the table-aware wrapper. Pass exactly one `cell`, `header`, or `footer` object:\n\n```ts\nconst headerContent = header.isPlaceholder ? null : FlexRender({ header })\nconst cellContent = FlexRender({ cell })\nconst footerContent = FlexRender({ footer: header })\n```\n\nFor cells, it selects `aggregatedCell` for aggregated rows, falls back to `cell`, and returns `null` for grouping placeholders.\n\n`flexRender` is the lower-level function for a renderable definition and its context:\n\n```ts\nconst content = flexRender(cell.column.columnDef.cell, cell.getContext())\n```\n\nIt invokes a function definition with the supplied props and passes any other value through unchanged. It does not select grouped-cell definitions or suppress placeholders.\n\nNeither helper inserts content into the document. Handle the returned value according to your rendering system. For example, assign trusted text to `textContent`, append a returned node, or pass a framework-specific value to another renderer. Do not assign untrusted strings to `innerHTML` without sanitizing them.\n\nPlaceholder headers and footers remain the caller's layout decision. Skip `header.isPlaceholder` in ordinary layouts unless a spanning-header layout intentionally needs that content.\n"}
